entially heading  the direction of a trial of an  impeachment trial this is why this stuff  matters and this is why taking over the  Senate and although it's an uphill  battle in 2020 or maybe in 2022 that's  why this stuff really matters I believe  that there is no question Donald Trump  will make the case that because of some  unfair treatment either in the context  of the impeachment inquiry or the  election or whatever Trump will make the  case that he didn't really lose or that  someone cheated or that this was rigged  or this that that was rigged her the  other thing I think it is less likely  that he will actually try to declare  martial law and I think it is almost an  impossibility that he would be able to  get away with it  but things have happened for the first  time before I mean think about other  times martial law has been declared in  the United States is very limited I  think after Pearl Harbor was bombed  martial law was declared and if I have  my history correct I almost don't want  to say but I think that that was related  to the internment camps of Japanese  Americans but the instances in which  martial law was was declared are  extraordinarily limited and the idea  that a House and Senate would allow  particularly when not controlled by  Trump's party that the House and Senate  would allow Trump to declare martial law  because he thinks the election against  him was unfair that the election that  went against him was unfair seems  extremely unlikely but I'm willing to  have my mind changed
 

